@startuml
!theme sunlust

abstract class Builder {
    + {abstract} buildPartA() : void
    + {abstract} buildPartB() : void
    + {abstract} buildPartC() : void
}

class ConcreteBuilder1 {
    - product : Product
    + buildPartA() : void
    + buildPartB() : void
    + buildPartC() : void
    + getProduct() : Product
    + reset() : void
}

class ConcreteBuilder2 {
    - product : Product
    + buildPartA() : void
    + buildPartB() : void
    + buildPartC() : void
    + getProduct() : Product
    + reset() : void
}

class Director {
    - builder : Builder*
    + setBuilder(Builder*) : void
    + buildMinimalViableProduct() : void
    + buildFullFeaturedProduct() : void
}

class Product {
    - parts : vector<string>
    + addPart(string) : void
    + listParts() : void
}

Builder <|-- ConcreteBuilder1
Builder <|-- ConcreteBuilder2

Director o--> Builder : uses

ConcreteBuilder1 ..> Product : creates
ConcreteBuilder2 ..> Product : creates

note right of Builder
    Declares product construction
    steps common to all builders
end note

note right of Director
    Defines the order of building steps.
    Works with builders through
    the common interface.
end note

note right of ConcreteBuilder1
    Provides specific implementation
    of the building steps.
    Constructs and assembles parts.
end note

note bottom of Product
    The complex object being built.
    Can have different representations
    based on the builder used.
end note

@enduml